WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.020
As you're probably aware, many Game of Thrones
fans were upset about how the show ended.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.179
After nearly a decade on television — and
following seven largely fantastic seasons

00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:12.020
— the acclaimed fantasy-drama delivered
a controversial swan song: a season that many

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.580
viewers thought was rushed, unsatisfying,
and really something of a mess.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.240
Contention over the final season came to a
head when one upset fan wrote a petition demanding

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.720
that HBO remake all six episodes with brand-new
writers.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.060
For some fans, It's hard not to roll your
eyes.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.360
The petition reads in part:

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.620
"David Benioff and D.B. Weiss have proven
themselves to be woefully incompetent writers."

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.140
More than 1.7 million disgruntled Game of
Thrones fans signed the petition, but those

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.020
efforts were reportedly made in vain.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.160
Basically, if you think the network is planning
to remake the season, we've got news for you.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.850
According to Entertainment Weekly, HBO president
of programming Casey Bloys addressed the online

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.260
petition during the Television Critics Association's
summer press tour:

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.400
"There are very few downsides to having a
hugely popular show.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.730
One I can think of, when you try to end it,
many people have opinions on how to end it.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.400
I think that comes with the territory.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.520
The petition shows a lot of enthusiasm and
passion for the show, but it wasn't something

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.720
we seriously considered.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.530
I can't imagine another network would."

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:15.700
Bloys also mentioned that HBO really doesn't
have too much creative control when it comes

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.160
to a hit show like Game of Thrones.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.080
In regards to the final season, he said,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.820
"There is a rhythm between showrunners and
network, a minimal back-and-forth here and

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.320
there.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.540
That’s not just GoT.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.220
Silicon Valley is doing their final season,
they have a really good handle on what the

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.740
show is and what the end will look like.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.300
It’s not like we are all over them.”

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:34.780
As for Game of Thrones, it sounds like Bloys
wasn't terribly surprised by the negative

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.280
reaction.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.240
After the final episode aired back in May,
he told Variety:

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:42.400
"I think to a certain extent it was expected
that for a show this big, there's no way you're

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:43.540
going to please everybody.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.189
[…] I think [Benioff and Weiss] landed a
massive plane and did a great job doing it.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:50.140
But you're never going to make everybody happy,
nor should that be the goal."

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:54.180
Meanwhile, some former Game of Thrones cast
members were evidently quite displeased about

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:54.680
the petition.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.240
Sophie Turner, the actress who played Sansa
Stark, found it particularly upsetting, telling

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.120
The New York Times:

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.510
"People always have an idea in their heads
of how they want a show to finish, and so

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.070
when it doesn't go to their liking, they start
to speak up about it and rebel.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:10.440
[...] All of these petitions and things like
that — I think it's disrespectful to the

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.669
crew, and the writers, and the filmmakers
who have worked tirelessly over 10 years,

00:02:14.669 --> 00:02:16.600
and for 11 months shooting the last season."

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.819
Isaac Hempstead Wright, who portrayed Bran
Stark, told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:22.549
"I saw today there's a petition to redo the
ending.

00:02:22.549 --> 00:02:23.540
[...] It's just absurd.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.900
I can't even fathom it.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.120
It's just ridiculous.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.280
It's ridiculous that people think they can
just demand a different ending because they

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.240
don't like it."

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.740
Jon Snow actor Kit Harington didn't mince
words when asked about the petition, telling

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:35.240
Esquire:

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.440
"I don't mean to sound mean about critics
here — but whatever critic spends half an

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.290
hour writing about this season and makes their
[negative] judgement on it, in my head they

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.460
can go f--- themselves.

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:47.040
[...] In the end, no one's bigger fans of
the show than we are, and we're kind of doing

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.840
it for ourselves.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.080
That's all we could do, really.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.800
And I was just happy we got to the end."

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:55.400
Clearly the folks at HBO realize that no matter
what you put out there, there's just no pleasing

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:55.900
everyone.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.980
At the end of the day, some audience members
will always react with shock and dismay.

